/P 215 0 R
/E (Before interviewing anyone, I checked the BCIT subreddit, mostly out of curiosity, and found people actively venting about the platform without me even asking. That told me something important early on: this wasn't a minor annoyance a few people had; it was widespread enough that students were bringing it up unprompted. That shaped whom I wanted to talk to.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (I interviewed three different groups: current students who use MyBCIT regularly, graduates who remembered what it used to be like, and people who'd never seen the platform before. That last group mattered more than I expected. Current students had gotten used to workarounds without realizing it, so the only way to really test how approachable the interface was meant to be was by bringing in someone with completely fresh eyes.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
