322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 218 0 R
/T (That convergence was the whole redesign brief, really. If five different complaints all point to the same root cause, being buried and hard to reach, then the fix isn't five separate features; it's one priority: get key information in front of people faster. That's really Hick's Law in practice: the more choices and steps someone has to wade through, the longer and harder a decision becomes. Cutting click depth wasn't just a nice metric to report; it was directly reducing that cognitive load. Alongside that, the visual system needed to feel like it belonged to 2024, not two decades ago.)
/E (That convergence was the whole redesign brief, really. If five different complaints all point to the same root cause, being buried and hard to reach, then the fix isn't five separate features; it's one priority: get key information in front of people faster. That's really Hick's Law in practice: the more choices and steps someone has to wade through, the longer and harder a decision becomes. Cutting click depth wasn't just a nice metric to report; it was directly reducing that cognitive load. Alongside that, the visual system needed to feel like it belonged to 2024, not two decades ago.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
