/T (Accessibility came from a similar place: listening rather than assuming. Testing surfaced something I hadn't fully anticipated: several participants specifically needed larger text and stronger contrast to comfortably use the platform. Once that came up, I checked the colour pairings against WCAG contrast guidelines directly, rather than relying on gut feeling, since "looks fine to me" isn't the same as actually meeting a real accessibility standard. That wasn't a nice-to-have I added at the end; it reshaped earlier decisions about type scale and colour pairing well before the visual design was finalized.)
/E (Accessibility came from a similar place: listening rather than assuming. Testing surfaced something I hadn't fully anticipated: several participants specifically needed larger text and stronger contrast to comfortably use the platform. Once that came up, I checked the colour pairings against WCAG contrast guidelines directly, rather than relying on gut feeling, since "looks fine to me" isn't the same as actually meeting a real accessibility standard. That wasn't a nice-to-have I added at the end; it reshaped earlier decisions about type scale and colour pairing well before the visual design was finalized.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
