1226 0 obj
<<
/Title (I'd used MyBCIT for years without really questioning it; it was just the thing you complained about and moved past. This project forced me to actually sit with that frustration instead of shrugging at it, and trace it back to specific, fixable decisions rather than a vague sense that it was "bad.")
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1215 0 R
/Next 1227 0 R
>>
endobj
1227 0 obj
<<
/Title (None of the individual changes were dramatic. Fewer clicks to grades, larger text, consolidated navigation, on paper that's a modest list. But testing showed those small changes were the whole difference between a platform people tolerated and one they'd actually call approachable. That's probably the biggest thing this project taught me: the most important design decisions are often the least visible ones, the stuff nobody notices until it's finally fixed.)
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1215 0 R
/Prev 1226 0 R
>>
endobj
